g.</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4322.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>She tried to go through the &lt;b&gt;checkout&lt;/b&gt; at the supermarket without paying.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Allegations of a  [cover-up] of the long-term effects of industrial pollution have been denied by the Environment Minister.</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4323.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Allegations of a  &lt;b&gt;cover-up&lt;/b&gt; of the long-term effects of industrial pollution have been denied by the Environment Minister.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The [intake] of students this year has fallen by 5% as a result of cuts in government funding to the universities.</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4324.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The &lt;b&gt;intake&lt;/b&gt; of students this year has fallen by 5% as a result of cuts in government funding to the universities.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Stephanie King was one of the four directors of the company who led a management [buyout] in 2010. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4325.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Stephanie King was one of the four directors of the company who led a management &lt;b&gt;buyout&lt;/b&gt; in 2010. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Weeks of demonstrations against the present economic policies have turned into a popular [uprising] against the military government.</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4326.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Weeks of demonstrations against the present economic policies have turned into a popular &lt;b&gt;uprising&lt;/b&gt; against the military government.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>A [breakdown] in communication between the publisher and the printer led to a misunderstanding and only 2,000 copies of the book were produced rather than 20,000. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4327.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>A &lt;b&gt;breakdown&lt;/b&gt; in communication between the publisher and the printer led to a misunderstanding and only 2,000 copies of the book were produced rather than 20,000. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>There are two [handouts] for this lecture: one contains an outline, and the other a list of further reading. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4328.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>There are two &lt;b&gt;handouts&lt;/b&gt; for this lecture: one contains an outline, and the other a list of further reading. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>He had a very sheltered [upbringing], and his parents didn't like him to go out of the house alone.  </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/4329.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>He had a very sheltered &lt;b&gt;upbringing&lt;/b&gt;, and his parents didn't like him to go out of the house alone.  </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Of all the possible [outcomes] of the Mars exploration project, they hadn't expected to find plant life on the planet. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/43210.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Of all the possible &lt;b&gt;outcomes&lt;/b&gt; of the Mars exploration project, they hadn't expected to find plant life on the planet. </modelAnswerString></question></question_xml><enableAudioOnChecked>false</enableAudioOnChecked><enableAudioOnClosed>true</enableAudioOnClosed><correctFeedback_str /><incorrectFeedback_str /><attemptsAllowed>1</attemptsAllowed></mcq_xml></params_xml><alignment>none</alignment><alignPercent>100</alignPercent><custom_style_name /><sharedTokenBankId /><is_sequential>False</is_sequential><is_compulsory>False</is_compulsory><states><state id="queued" visible="True" enabled="False" /><state id="in_progress" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="complete" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="checked" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="closed" visible="True" enabled="True" /></states></params></object><object linkID="background_image"><params><